{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-13c37048-ccae-4277-8753-62044e59c6dc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a57f08994931f9d0","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-lpattpc9/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E002.md","content":"# Investigate artifact path resolvability for workspace validation\n\n## Description\n\nResolve whether artifact request paths handled by the MLflow artifacts-only server carry sufficient information (experiment ID or run ID) to resolve workspace membership. The strategy's design resolves each artifact path to its parent experiment (artifacts stored under experiment-scoped paths, e.g. `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`), looks up the experiment's workspace assignment via the workspace store, and delegates authorization to the existing auth plugin infrastructure. The strategy flags this assumption as needing validation and carries the risk that artifact paths may not straightforwardly map to experiment IDs in all artifact storage backends or custom artifact root configurations. If the assumption does not hold, the server's workspace-validation approach must be rewritten; the investigation therefore gates the server implementation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Trace how the artifacts-only proxy parses and serves artifact request paths (the `/api/2.0/mlflow/artifacts/*` endpoints) in the MLflow server source.\n- Validate that, for the S3 artifact store with the standard `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` layout (the standard RHOAI configuration), each artifact request path form resolves to a parent experiment ID.\n- Determine how run-ID-only path forms (if any) resolve to experiment and thereby workspace membership.\n- Document artifact root configurations where resolution is not possible, and specify the required behavior for them (request denied, consistent with the fail-closed design).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given artifact request paths from the artifacts-only API surface, when parsed per the S3 standard layout, then each path form's resolvability to an experiment (and thereby a workspace) is classified, measured by a documented path-form inventory with a resolvable/unresolvable determination per form.\n- Given unresolvable path forms, the required handling (request denied — fail-closed) is specified for the implementation, measured by a written recommendation.\n- Limitations for non-standard artifact roots are documented, measured by a limitations note usable as implementation input.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Gates the P0 HLRs \"Artifact requests ... are validated against workspace membership; requests from users without workspace membership are denied with HTTP 403\" and \"Workspace-aware artifact serving is fail-closed\" by validating the path-resolution assumption those HLRs build on.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":73453,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88698f900cb0bd7f","agent_id":"a1b8946567b2496a2","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"9795c021-59f4-449e-bf56-d84a5bc84174","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:14:51.885Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
