{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0bafc44b-4c53-4471-b899-5041ffac2f2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-96f5521454ef012c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-lpattpc9/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E003.md","content":"# Investigate split-topology artifact traffic routing mechanism\n\n## Description\n\nResolve how the main MLflow tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. The strategy poses this as an open question owned by the MLflow Team: the answer affects the HTTPRoute design and determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. The outcome selects between two conditional downstream implementations, so it gates the operator topology work and determines which routing epic exists.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Analyze the artifact API request paths served by the main tracking deployment versus the dedicated artifacts-only instance, based on the MLflow server source and the operator's existing routing resources.\n- Determine whether Gateway API HTTPRoute path-based rules (consistent with the operator's existing conditional CRD discovery pattern for optional dependencies) can route artifact API traffic to the dedicated instance with no tracking-server change.\n- Determine what tracking-server-side change (configuration or code) would be needed if gateway-level routing is insufficient to delegate artifact operations.\n- Produce a decision record selecting the routing mechanism, with the HTTPRoute design implications and main tracking deployment configuration implications.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A bounded outcome is recorded — gateway-level routing sufficient, or tracking-server delegation required — measured by a written decision with supporting analysis.\n- The selected mechanism's implications for HTTPRoute design and for the main tracking deployment configuration are documented, measured by a design note usable as implementation input.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Gates the P1 HLR \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\" by selecting the mechanism through which that HLR is realized.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":74111,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88698f900cb0bd7f","agent_id":"a1b8946567b2496a2","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"266b9dd5-ae6d-4852-a02c-8e695b06b926","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:15:00.368Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
