{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-90f3e0ac-2067-4563-ae4f-c21b3f3fc14c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-88a87b516cc0fdf9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-lpattpc9/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E007.md","content":"# Fail-mode analysis of workspace-aware artifact serving\n\n## Description\n\nEnumerate and classify the failure modes of workspace-aware artifact serving, confirming fail-closed coverage. The strategy specifies fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable, but the full failure-mode surface of the artifacts-only serving path and the split-server topology — unresolvable artifact paths, plugin initialization failures, workspace store errors and timeouts, malformed requests, and partial topology misconfiguration — must be enumerated with a defined required behavior for each. Any mode where the specified design would not fail closed requires additional remediation work in the server implementation, so this analysis gates it. This investigation exists because the strategy is a safety-critical, multi-tenant access-control change (workspace/tenant isolation with fail-closed authorization).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enumerate failure modes across the workspace-aware artifact serving path: workspace store unreachable or erroring, artifact paths that do not resolve to an experiment, auth plugin initialization failure, malformed or ambiguous requests, and partial split-topology misconfiguration (e.g. an artifacts-only instance deployed without workspace flags).\n- For each mode, define the required behavior (deny with the appropriate status and log, or serve) consistent with the fail-closed design: transient infrastructure failures must not silently degrade tenant isolation.\n- Identify any modes where the specified design would serve artifacts without validation, and propose remediation scope for them.\n- Deliverable: a failure-mode matrix with required behaviors and a remediation list (empty if none).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every enumerated failure mode has a defined required behavior and response, measured by a complete failure-mode matrix.\n- Any mode where the current design would not fail closed is identified with proposed remediation, measured by a documented remediation list (which may be empty if the design is confirmed fail-closed across all modes).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Covers and validates the P0 HLR \"Workspace-aware artifact serving is fail-closed: if the workspace store is unreachable, requests are denied\" and supports the P0 workspace-membership validation HLR by confirming denial behavior across all failure modes.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":74625,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88698f900cb0bd7f","agent_id":"a1b8946567b2496a2","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"19f11469-7234-4799-bb65-22d02b008c63","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:15:10.631Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
