consistent with workspace-aware serving for denials and unavailable validation.\n- Given non-artifact API requests (tracking, model registry, prompt registry), they continue to be served by the main tracking deployment, measured by those operations functioning unchanged.\n- Given a cluster without Gateway API CRDs, routing degrades consistently with the operator's conditional CRD discovery pattern, measured by no reconciliation failure.\n- The routing design matches the decision record produced by the routing mechanism investigation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P1: Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (this branch's realization of that HLR, when gateway-level routing is the selected mechanism).\n\n## Gate Failure Impact\n\nIf the routing investigation finds gateway-level routing insufficient, this epic is removed and the tracking-server delegation branch applies instead.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":79126,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88698f900cb0bd7f","agent_id":"a1b8946567b2496a2","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"0d41317c-dc10-49c9-bc90-d602bf16c794","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:16:19.024Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
