rved by the main tracking server, measured by those operations functioning unchanged.\n- The delegation design matches the decision record produced by the routing mechanism investigation.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P1: Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (this branch's realization of that HLR, when tracking-server delegation is the selected mechanism).\n\n## Gate Failure Impact\n\nIf the routing investigation finds gateway-level routing sufficient with no tracking-server change, this epic is removed and the gateway-level routing branch applies instead.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":79753,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88698f900cb0bd7f","agent_id":"a1b8946567b2496a2","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"e9f31156-ca4e-4b11-8ba8-61e9f8dc02ef","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:16:27.570Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
