{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ead2c06d8cd7c86","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: Investigate workspace-resolution initialization coupling in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate workspace-resolution initialization coupling in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve whether the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace provider and its workspace resolution logic can be initialized and exercised in an MLflow server running in artifacts-only mode, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The strategy flags (open question, the \"Auth plugin coupling to full server initialization\" risk, and the assumption that the workspace store provides experiment-to-workspace mapping accessible without initializing tracking stores) that workspace resolution may currently be coupled to the full tracking server initialization path. The answer determines whether the plugin work for the artifacts-only context is a verification-only change or requires refactoring workspace resolution into an independent initialization path — it changes the scope of the plugin implementation work.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Trace the plugin's workspace provider registration (the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group, loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) and its initialization dependencies in the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins source.\n34\t- Determine whether workspace store initialization (`kubernetes://` URI scheme) or experiment-to-workspace resolution reads tracking store or model registry state.\n35\t- Identify the minimal initialization path required for workspace resolution to function with tracking and model registry stores uninitialized.\n36\t- Produce a findings report: coupled or not coupled, the specific dependencies involved, and — if coupled — the refactor scope for factoring workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- Given the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins source, when the workspace provider initialization path is traced, then every dependency it requires (workspace store, tracking store, model registry store, other services) is enumerated, measured by a documented dependency inventory.\n41\t- Given the findings, a clear coupled/not-coupled determination is recorded with code-level evidence, measured by a written conclusion referencing the specific initialization path.\n42\t- If coupled, the refactor scope (independent initialization path for workspace resolution) is described including the affected plugin modules; if not coupled, verification evidence that workspace resolution succeeds without tracking store initialization is documented.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- Covers the P1 HLR \"Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization\" by resolving the unknown that determines the scope of that implementation work.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab99201f8d919049","agent_id":"adde90d1badb39ce7","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"b8e4df01-cd4e-4991-83cc-b9924b410b8d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:20:12.082Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ead2c06d8cd7c86","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"sub