{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98d7973e2f6aeaa3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: Investigate split-topology artifact traffic routing mechanism\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate split-topology artifact traffic routing mechanism\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve how the main MLflow tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. The strategy poses this as an open question owned by the MLflow Team: the answer affects the HTTPRoute design and determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. The outcome selects between two conditional downstream implementations, so it gates the operator topology work and determines which routing epic exists.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Analyze the artifact API request paths served by the main tracking deployment versus the dedicated artifacts-only instance, based on the MLflow server source and the operator's existing routing resources.\n34\t- Determine whether Gateway API HTTPRoute path-based rules (consistent with the operator's existing conditional CRD discovery pattern for optional dependencies) can route artifact API traffic to the dedicated instance with no tracking-server change.\n35\t- Determine what tracking-server-side change (configuration or code) would be needed if gateway-level routing is insufficient to delegate artifact operations.\n36\t- Produce a decision record selecting the routing mechanism, with the HTTPRoute design implications and main tracking deployment configuration implications.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A bounded outcome is recorded — gateway-level routing sufficient, or tracking-server delegation required — measured by a written decision with supporting analysis.\n41\t- The selected mechanism's implications for HTTPRoute design and for the main tracking deployment configuration are documented, measured by a design note usable as implementation input.\n42\t\n43\t## HLR Traceability\n44\t\n45\t- Gates the P1 HLR \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\" by selecting the mechanism through which that HLR is realized.\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab99201f8d919049","agent_id":"adde90d1badb39ce7","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"0be9b5a8-7a96-4134-ae1a-6944cfec6b7a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:20:18.579Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-98d7973e2f6aeaa3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
