{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a81b1ac523f0a607","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: Split-server artifacts-only topology in the MLflow operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E008\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the routing investigation selects tracking-server delegation,\n16\t    the HTTPRoute design for the dedicated instance is rewritten accordingly; remediation\n17\t    items from the security bypass analysis for split-topology misconfiguration are\n18\t    incorporated.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 6\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Split-server artifacts-only topology in the MLflow operator\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tDeploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — a split-server topology in which the main tracking deployment handles experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. This is not a configuration toggle (Staff Engineer direction): the operator renders new Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute using its existing Helm-in-operator pattern (MLflow CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via Server-Side Apply). The operator propagates workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms it already uses for the main tracking deployment, and manages the split topology declaratively so users configure a single MLflow CR. Gateway API HTTPRoute resources are created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n41\t\n42\tThis epic is gated by the investigation selecting the artifact traffic routing mechanism (which affects HTTPRoute design) and by the security bypass analysis (which covers split-topology misconfiguration vectors). The routing of artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to this dedicated instance is implemented separately, per the mechanism that investigation selects. The workspace-aware artifacts-only server capability is developed in parallel in the MLflow server repository — the deployed image's support for the combined flags is a configuration reference verified by acceptance criteria, not a build dependency.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- New Helm chart templates: artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, separate from the main tracking Deployment's resources.\n47\t- Propagation of workspace configuration flags to the artifacts-only instance using the same mechanisms as the main tracking deployment.\n48\t- Reconciliation of the split topology from a single MLflow CR (declarative management of two Deployments, two Services, two HTTPRoutes).\n49\t- Operator validation rejecting configurations where the artifacts-only instance would be deployed without workspace flags (misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation).\n50\t- Conditional HTTPRoute creation via runtime CRD discovery (no hard Gateway API dependency).\n51\t- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, when the operator reconciles the CR, then the operator creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n56\t- Given the dedicated artifacts-only instance deployed by the operator, the artifacts-only Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`, measured by inspecting the container command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n57\t- Given an MLflow CR requesting an artifacts-only instance without workspace configuration, the operator rejects the invalid configuration, measured by a validation error on the CR.\n58\t- Given a cluster without Gateway API CRDs, the operator reconciles without creating HTTPRoutes and without failing, measured by behavior consistent with the existing conditional CRD discovery pattern.\n59\t- The image deployed for the artifacts-only instance supports the combined workspace-aware flags, measured by verifying the rendered deployment against the MLflow server capability at execution time.\n60\t- Remediation items identified by the security bypass analysis for split-topology misconfiguration vectors are incorporated.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- P1: MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n65\t- Supports the P1 HLR \"Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\" (the routing implementation consumes the dedicated instance this epic deploys).\n66\t\n67\t## Risks\n68\t\n69\t- Split-deployment operational complexity (strategy risk): two Deployments, two Services, two HTTPRoutes and routing configuration increase the operational surface; mitigated by declarative single-CR management and operator validation rejecting artifacts-only configurations that lack workspace flags.\n70\t- Helm chart extensibility (strategy assumption, needs validation): the chart is expected to support a second Deployment without structural changes to the chart architecture; if structural changes are needed they are handled within this epic.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab99201f8d919049","agent_id":"adde90d1badb39ce7","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"f05c10ad-f9bf-44e1-919f-bdf9ab16aaa4","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:20:29.244Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a81b1ac523f0a607","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
