orkspace-aware artifact serving | Investigation | MLflow Team | P0 |\n30\t\n31\t### Conditional branch epics (attached to E003, not standalone Jira issues)\n32\t\n33\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Branch |\n34\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|--------|\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-A-E009 | Gateway-level artifact traffic routing to the dedicated artifacts-only instance | Implementation | MLflow Team | P1 | A |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E009 | Tracking-server artifact delegation to the dedicated artifacts-only instance | Implementation | MLflow Team | P1 | B |\n37\t\n38\t## Dependency DAG (main plan)\n39\t\n40\t```mermaid\n41\tgraph TD\n42\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-8009-E001] --> E005[RHAISTRAT-8009-E005]\n43\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-8009-E002] --> E004[RHAISTRAT-8009-E004]\n44\t    E005[RHAISTRAT-8009-E005] --> E004[RHAISTRAT-8009-E004]\n45\t    E007[RHAISTRAT-8009-E007] --> E004[RHAISTRAT-8009-E004]\n46\t    E008[RHAISTRAT-8009-E008] --> E004[RHAISTRAT-8009-E004]\n47\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-8009-E003] --> E006[RHAISTRAT-8009-E006]\n48\t    E008[RHAISTRAT-8009-E008] --> E006[RHAISTRAT-8009-E006]\n49\t```\n50\t\n51\t### Conditional branches from E003\n52\t\n53\t```mermaid\n54\tgraph TD\n55\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-8009-E003] --> BA[RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-A-E009]\n56\t    E003 --> BB[RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E009]\n57\t    E006[RHAISTRAT-8009-E006] --> BA\n58\t    E006 --> BB\n59\t```\n60\t\n61\tOnly one branch is realized, depending on the E003 outcome. Branch epics are excluded from the main-plan critical path.\n62\t\n63\t## DAG Justification\n64\t\n65\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n66\t|------|------|-----------|\n67\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | Open question \"Does workspace store initialization in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins depend on tracking store availability?\" determines whether the plugin work is verification-only or requires refactoring workspace resolution into an independent initialization path — scope/approach gate (`rewrite`). |\n68\t| E001 → E005 (existence) | Rule 3 | The unknown is strategy-flagged (open question, risk \"Auth plugin coupling to full server initialization\", assumption \"workspace store accessible without initializing tracking stores\") and its answer changes what the plugin epic does. |\n69\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 3 | Assumption \"artifact request paths include sufficient information to resolve workspace membership\" is flagged needs-validation; if paths do not resolve, the server's workspace-validation approach rewrites (`rewrite` gate). |\n70\t| E005 → E004 | Rule 12 (library → consumer serial) | The MLflow server's artifacts-only workspace validation builds against the plugin's workspace resolution (loaded via `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point / WorkspaceStoreRegistry). If the plugin's initialization path is refactored, the server-side wiring consumes that change. |\n71\t| E007 → E004 | Rule 19 (safety-critical: fail-mode Investigation) | Workspace-aware artifact serving is a multi-tenant access-control feature (tenant isolation, fail-closed authorization). The fail-mode analysis enumerates failure modes and confirms fail-closed coverage; may reveal modes requiring additional remediation (`add_remediation` gate). |\n72\t| E008 → E004 | Rule 19 (safety-critical: security Investigation) | Bypass-vector analysis (crafted paths, direct instance access) gates the main server implementation; may reveal remediation work (`add_remediation` gate). |\n73\t| E003 → E006 | Rule 3 | Open question \"How should the operator configure artifact traffic routing?\" — answer \"affects HTTPRoute design\", so the operator topology epic is gated (`rewrite`). |\n74\t| E008 → E006 | Rule 19 | Risk \"Split-deployment operational complexity\" states misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation; the security analysis covers operator misconfiguration vectors and gates the topology implementation (`add_remediation` gate). |\n75\t| E003 → branch epics | Rule 3 (bounded outcomes → conditional branches) | Two bounded outcomes: (A) gateway-level routing suffices; (B) tracking-server delegation required. Each outcome selects a different branch epic (`remove` gate on the non-selected branch). |\n76\t| E006 → branch epics | Rule 12/13 | Both routing branches configure traffic toward the dedicated artifacts-only instance; they consume the deployed instance produced by the operator topology epic. |\n77\t| E001 ∥ E002 ∥ E003 ∥ E007 ∥ E008 | Rule 14 (parallel) | Independent investigations resolving distinct unknowns (plugin init coupling, path resolvability, routing mechanism, failure modes, bypass vectors); no shared deliverable — not combined. |\n78\t| E004 ∥ E006 (no edge) | Rule 14 + Rule 13 clarification | Different repos (mlflow vs mlflow-operator); the operator renders Helm templates referencing server flags — a configuration reference, not a build-against artifact. Verified by AC (\"deployed image supports the combined flags\"), never a DAG edge. |\n79\t| Branch epics ∥ E004 (no edge) | Rules 14/15 | Routing configuration does not build against the server's workspace-validation code (different repos / different areas in the same repo); end-to-end routing validation is an AC gate, not a DAG dependency. |\n80\t| No docs-authoring epic | Step 5 rule 11 boundary | Documentation Support is \"Pending human review\" (not Yes) and no substantive content authoring is in scope; incidental doc touch-ups (documenting limitations for non-standard artifact roots) stay inside the originating epics as scope/AC. |\n81\t| No onboarding chain | Rule 20 N/A | MLflow and MLflow Operator have architecture context files and existing Konflux builds; mlflow-kubernetes-plugins is an existing internal component (see Health Warnings). |\n82\t\n83\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n84\t\n85\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n86\t|-----|----------|---------|\n87\t| `--artifacts-only` composable with `--enable-workspaces` and `--workspace-store-uri` | P0 | E004 |\n88\t| Artifac