nes which routing implementation exists and HTTPRoute design | E006 (rewrite); branch A/B epics (remove) |\n127\t| E007 | Failure-mode surface of workspace-aware serving | May reveal modes requiring remediation beyond specified fail-closed design | E004 (add_remediation) |\n128\t| E008 | Validation bypass vectors in split topology | May reveal unmitigated vectors requiring additional work in server/operator | E004, E006 (add_remediation) |\n129\t\n130\tOpen questions NOT promoted to Investigations (with handling):\n131\t- **Latency overhead / caching at launch** (PM/Engineering) — does not change which epics exist; captured as measurement + conditional short-TTL caching AC on E004. See Health Warnings.\n132\t- **Audit telemetry channel** (PM/Security) — HLR already specifies server logs; implemented as specified in E004, with scope-growth risk flagged in Health Warnings.\n133\t- Assumption \"flags composable without breaking init sequence\" — the work itself (E004); failure = fix within the epic.\n134\t- Assumption \"Helm chart supports a second Deployment without structural changes\" — the work itself (E006).\n135\t- Assumption \"single-tenant deployments do not set --enable-workspaces\" — backwards-compatibility AC on E004 (strategy HLR P0-4 requires current behavior preserved regardless).\n136\t\n137\t## Conditional Branches\n138\t\n139\tE003 (routing mechanism investigation) has two bounded outcomes that change downstream structure:\n140\t\n141\t- **Branch A — gateway-level routing suffices**: HTTPRoute path-based rules route artifact API traffic to the dedicated instance; no tracking-server change. Realized by `RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-A-E009` (MLflow Operator work).\n142\t- **Branch B — tracking-server delegation required**: the main tracking server needs a configuration/code change to delegate artifact operations. Realized by `RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E009` (MLflow server work).\n143\t\n144\tBoth branch epics set `branch`, `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-8009-E003` (also in `dependencies`), and `gate_failure_impact.action=remove`. No main-plan epic lists a branch epic in its dependencies.\n145\t\n146\t## Health Warnings\n147\t\n148\t1. **Priority observation (non-blocking)**: the P0 HLRs (server-side workspace-aware serving) only deliver user-facing value in multi-tenant deployments once the P1 operator topology (E006) and routing land. The P1 work sits on the value-realization path of the P0 scope — consider whether the operator epic should be pulled forward in planning.\n149\t2. **Performance NFR has no latency target**: the strategy's Performance NFR defers to an open PM/Engineering question. Caching-at-launch vs deferred is undetermined; handled as a measurement + conditional-caching AC on E004. May spawn follow-up work.\n150\t3. **Audit channel scope risk (P2)**: HLR-8 specifies server logs, but open question 4 (PM/Security) may expand the channel (OTLP, Kubernetes audit log). Implemented per HLR; scope growth would be a follow-up.\n151\t4. **mlflow-kubernetes-plugins not in architecture context**: no architecture context file exists for it, but the strategy's dependency table marks it \"internal, exists\" and mlflow.md documents it shipping in the MLflow image (v1.5.0, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`). Treated as an existing internal component — no repo-onboarding/konflux-onboarding chain generated. Flagged for human verification that the team's plugin repo is accessible for modification.\n152\t5. **Strategy-level process gates pending**: Architecture Review, Build Onboarding, Licence Validation, and other prerequisites are all \"Pending human review\" — outstanding human gates at the strategy level that may affect epic sequencing.\n153\t6. **Scope note (S3-only path resolution)**: per the strategy's risk mitigation, the initial implementation is scoped to the S3 artifact store with the standard `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` layout; limitations for non-standard artifact roots must be documented (AC on E004).\n154\t\n155\t## 