{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8eb8751c7bd0621f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Artifacts-only workspace resolution in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking server\n15\t    initialization path, this epic's scope expands from verification to refactoring\n16\t    workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin,\n17\t    per the investigation findings.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Artifacts-only workspace resolution in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tVerify and extend the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin so that workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The plugin, registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`, already provides experiment-to-workspace mapping for the tracking server's non-artifact operations. The artifacts-only server must be able to call the same workspace resolution logic before proxying artifact requests to the storage backend. If the workspace-resolution initialization coupling investigation finds that resolution depends on the full tracking server initialization path, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin. The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup are unchanged — authentication at the ingress level works identically for both the tracking server and the artifacts-only instance.\n40\t\n41\tThis epic is gated by the investigation resolving whether the plugin's workspace resolution is coupled to tracking store initialization, which determines whether this work is verification-only or requires refactoring.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Verify that the plugin's workspace resolution (experiment-to-workspace mapping, workspace store access via the `kubernetes://` URI scheme) initializes and functions in a server context with tracking and model registry stores uninitialized.\n46\t- If coupled to the full tracking server initialization path: factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin.\n47\t- Ensure workspace resolution can be driven from artifact request handling (resolving the experiment's workspace assignment for artifact paths delegated by the server), reusing the existing auth plugin infrastructure without dictating new Kubernetes API mechanics.\n48\t- Preserve existing plugin behavior for the full tracking server context — no regression to non-artifact workspace operations.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given an MLflow server in artifacts-only mode with workspace flags set, the plugin's workspace resolution initializes and resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping without tracking store initialization, measured by successful resolution in the artifacts-only context.\n53\t- Given the full tracking server context, existing plugin behavior is unchanged, measured by regression coverage of non-artifact workspace operations.\n54\t- Workspace authorization for artifact requests reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure (no new auth mechanism or server flag), measured by the plugin continuing to be loaded through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group.\n55\t- If a refactor was required, the independent initialization path is covered by tests demonstrating resolution with tracking/registry stores absent.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- P1: Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization.\n60\t- Enables (transitively) the P0 HLR: artifact requests through the workspace-aware artifacts-only server are validated against workspace membership with HTTP 403 denials — hence this epic inherits P0 priority.\n61\t\n62\t## Risks\n63\t\n64\t- Auth plugin coupling to full server initialization (strategy risk): if workspace resolution depends on stores that artifacts-only mode does not initialize, the refactor factors resolution into an independent initialization path — the gating investigation determines this scope before implementation begins.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-875a96a172fb2b4e","agent_id":"a83d4d905b3d9d722","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"5c344cdd-45f6-419b-bd03-b6b3daa396cb","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:31:09.663Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8eb8751c7bd0621f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
