{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-954c0b1cf0caae50","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E008\n3\ttitle: Security bypass analysis of workspace-aware artifact serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Security bypass analysis of workspace-aware artifact serving\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tAnalyze bypass vectors for workspace validation in the split-server topology. The strategy's \"Split-deployment operational complexity\" risk notes that a misconfigured split topology could result in artifact requests bypassing workspace validation, silently degrading tenant isolation. This investigation identifies and evaluates bypass vectors — crafted artifact paths that escape experiment scoping, direct access to the artifacts-only instance bypassing the intended routing, operator misconfiguration, and interactions with the unchanged kube-rbac-proxy authentication layer — and maps mitigations to the implementation work. Unmitigated vectors require additional remediation, so this analysis gates the server and operator implementations. This investigation exists because the strategy is a safety-critical, multi-tenant access-control change (workspace/tenant isolation).\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Threat analysis of the workspace validation path in the artifacts-only server: path manipulation and encoding tricks, paths that resolve to no experiment or to the wrong experiment, requests with missing or invalid workspace context.\n34\t- Network and routing bypass vectors in the split topology: direct access to the artifacts-only instance or its Service bypassing the intended entry point, HTTPRoute misrouting.\n35\t- Operator misconfiguration vectors: an artifacts-only instance deployed without workspace flags, workspace configuration not propagated.\n36\t- Confirm that the unchanged authentication layer (kube-rbac-proxy sidecar, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) behaves identically for the artifacts-only instance and cannot be used to skip authorization.\n37\t- Map each vector to a mitigation in the server implementation, the plugin, or operator validation; identify unmitigated vectors requiring additional work.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- Bypass vectors are enumerated with evaluated exploitability, measured by a documented threat analysis.\n42\t- Each vector is mapped to a mitigation or confirmed blocked by design, measured by a complete vector-to-mitigation matrix.\n43\t- Unmitigated vectors are identified with recommended remediation scope, measured by a documented remediation list (which may be empty).\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- Validates the P0 HLRs \"Artifact requests ... are validated against workspace membership; requests from users without workspace membership are denied with HTTP 403\" and \"Workspace-aware artifact serving is fail-closed\", and the Security NFR (all artifact access in workspace-aware mode validated through the existing auth plugin infrastructure; failure to validate results in access denial).\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-875a96a172fb2b4e","agent_id":"a83d4d905b3d9d722","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"5147d5e7-0c24-431b-bf4c-9e7652f1c6a2","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:31:15.208Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-954c0b1cf0caae50","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
