{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6a76ce1df619ef9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-A-E009\n3\ttitle: Gateway-level artifact traffic routing to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the routing investigation finds gateway-level routing insufficient,\n17\t    this epic is removed and the tracking-server delegation branch applies instead.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Gateway-level artifact traffic routing to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tConditional epic (branch A, selected if the artifact traffic routing mechanism investigation finds gateway-level routing sufficient): configure Gateway API HTTPRoute path-based routing so that artifact API traffic entering through the main tracking deployment's route is routed to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, with no tracking-server change. The split-server topology's dedicated instance (Deployment, Service, HTTPRoute) is deployed by the operator topology work; this epic implements the routing mechanism on top of it.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- HTTPRoute path rules routing artifact API request paths to the dedicated artifacts-only instance's Service, per the design selected by the routing investigation.\n43\t- Any main-route or gateway configuration needed to split artifact traffic from tracking traffic at the ingress layer.\n44\t- Routing configuration follows the operator's existing conditional Gateway API CRD discovery pattern for optional dependencies.\n45\t- End-to-end validation that artifact requests routed through the main entry point reach the dedicated instance and are subject to workspace validation there (coordinated with the workspace-aware artifacts-only serving capability developed in the MLflow server repository).\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Given a user requesting an artifact through the main tracking entry point, the request is served by the dedicated artifacts-only instance with workspace validation applied, measured by HTTP 200 for authorized workspace members and HTTP 403/503 responses consistent with workspace-aware serving for denials and unavailable validation.\n50\t- Given non-artifact API requests (tracking, model registry, prompt registry), they continue to be served by the main tracking deployment, measured by those operations functioning unchanged.\n51\t- Given a cluster without Gateway API CRDs, routing degrades consistently with the operator's conditional CRD discovery pattern, measured by no reconciliation failure.\n52\t- The routing design matches the decision record produced by the routing mechanism investigation.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- P1: Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (this branch's realization of that HLR, when gateway-level routing is the selected mechanism).\n57\t\n58\t## Gate Failure Impact\n59\t\n60\tIf the routing investigation finds gateway-level routing insufficient, this epic is removed and the tracking-server delegation branch applies instead.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-875a96a172fb2b4e","agent_id":"a83d4d905b3d9d722","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"1271