icated artifacts-only instance, per the mechanism identified by the routing investigation.\n44\t- Preserve non-artifact operations (experiment tracking, model registry, prompt registry) on the main tracking server — no changes to workspace isolation for non-artifact operations.\n45\t- End-to-end validation that delegated artifact requests are subject to workspace validation at the dedicated instance.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Given a user requesting an artifact through the main tracking server, the request is delegated to the dedicated artifacts-only instance and subject to workspace validation, measured by HTTP 200 for authorized workspace members and HTTP 403/503 responses consistent with workspace-aware serving for denials and unavailable validation.\n50\t- Given non-artifact API requests (tracking, model registry, prompt registry), they continue to be served by the main tracking server, measured by those operations functioning unchanged.\n51\t- The delegation design matches the decision record produced by the routing mechanism investigation.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- P1: Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance (this branch's realization of that HLR, when tracking-server delegation is the selected mechanism).\n56\t\n57\t## Gate Failure Impact\n58\t\n59\tIf the routing investigation finds gateway-level routing sufficient with no tracking-server change, this epic is removed and the gateway-level routing branch applies instead.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-875a96a172fb2b4e","agent_id":"a83d4d905b3d9d722","session_id":"1a623240-3c0b-475a-b0a3-8024f6d16813","uuid":"af6f2cfb-a1a1-46de-bc9b-7b2fa168a28b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:31:19.602Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad8207b3df35ed2f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
